  "explanation_result": {
    "decision": "EXPLAINED",
    "explanation": "The +4.6% jump on 2025\u201108\u201115 was driven by fresh news of tightening Brazil supply and heightened trade barriers. Two days earlier, analysts warned that frost and drought in Brazil were slashing output and exports, creating a supply shortfall (source: 9db4147b9b9a95c2; 7d952a6445a2a878). On 2025\u201108\u201114, reports highlighted the impact of newly\u2011imposed U.S. tariffs on Brazilian coffee, which were already pushing prices higher (source: 7ee7713983737c3c). The same day, a Reuters piece noted that U.S. coffee buyers were seeking to postpone Brazil shipments, further constraining immediate supply (source: e65439ac6158ed67). Finally, a same\u2011day news recap confirmed that the United States was delaying Brazil shipments, reinforcing market expectations of reduced availability (source: 664164b10dc42538). Together, these timely supply\u2011side shocks explain the sharp price increase on 15\u202fAugust.",
